  "rejected_experiments": [
    {
      "name": "bulk preparation guard",
      "reason": "partial_account_allowance regression prepares only one body, serializing usable independent account capacity; retained code prepares six with ten overlapping first updates. Large-backlog regression prepares ten. No bulk guard is retained."
    },
    {
      "name": "fast-lane IDLE default",
      "reason": "fewer empty fast queries did not establish reliability/latency benefit; first trial 4/5 with header timeout, later combined trial had a long cohort outlier. Fast default remains polling."
    }
  ],
  "retained_failure_interpretation": [
    "Quiet TLS and distinct-account header failures in intermediate cohorts are retained; successful repetitions do not erase them.",
    "Fluctuating account command-service model passes 2/3 before profiling; the failed case has a response-header timeout. The largest aggregate journal update predates that failed request and cannot explain its pause.",
    "Race CPU-profile cohort passes 2/3; its failure expires the original 5s HTTP body deadline. Race instrumentation dominates the profile, but this is not a qualification waiver.",
    "Initial timeline regression repeatedly closed a collected grant and got ErrMissing; corrected caller issues fresh grants.",
